<header><div class="kicker">Field development</div>
<h1>Concept and economic screening</h1>
<p class="sub">Draft for technical review</p></header>

<h2 id="summary">1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p>The field development module is a screening tool for offshore host concepts, costs,
layouts and production economics. Analysis is performed to determine how a documented
illustrative field is ranked and evaluated. The key results are summarized below.</p>
<ul><li>Concept shortlisting is supported under the stated heuristic assumptions.
<ul><li>Spar and Semi-submersible tie at {{score_Spar}} each. Stable legacy enumeration
order places {{selected}} first; the score does not establish a preference between them.
The tied alternative has a separate net present value of {{tied_npv}} million USD.
The water depth of
{{water_depth_m}} m lies within the selected {{selected}}'s implemented screening band of {{depth_low}} to
{{depth_high}} m. This is a model applicability check, not a structural capacity check.</li></ul></li>
<li>The calculated economic value is unsuitable for investment acceptance.
<ul><li>Pre-tax net present value is {{npv}} million USD, above the zero-value comparison
line. Scheduled production is {{production_mmbbl}} million barrels against the supplied
reservoir size of {{reservoir_size_mmbbl}} million barrels. The production discrepancy
prevents acceptance of that economic value.</li></ul></li></ul>
