<h2 id="introduction">2. Introduction</h2>
<p>Offshore development choices are screened using water depth, reservoir size, access to
existing infrastructure and fluid type. The selected host is passed into cost estimation
and annual cash-flow evaluation. The calculation described here is the documented public
workflow example, with its identifying label replaced by a neutral description.</p>
<p>The example is an illustration supplied with the software. It is not a measured field
dataset or a published independent benchmark. Its numerical inputs are read directly from
the documented example, and its results are obtained by calling the module. The source
editions and precise calculation locators are recorded in §9.2.</p>

<h2 id="controls">3. Summary of decision controls</h2>
<p>The screening output is used to organize further engineering evaluation. Acceptance is
conditioned on a reconciled production forecast, independently established cost inputs and
a verified fiscal basis.</p>
<p>A positive suitability score identifies a candidate for further consideration. It does
not establish technical feasibility. A positive net present value only describes the
discounted cash-flow balance under the supplied assumptions. The production-volume
discrepancy in this example overrides that financial comparison.</p>
<figure>{{chart}}<figcaption>Figure A. Pre-tax price sensitivity for the selected host.
The dashed line is the mathematical zero-value comparison, not an approval boundary.
Hover or keyboard focus identifies price, calculated value, component and limit.
The complete values are retained in Table C.</figcaption></figure>
<p>The curve holds concept, capacity, costs, discount rate and field life fixed. It does
not represent a price forecast. All plotted cases retain the unresolved production basis.</p>

<h2 id="basis">4. Design data and basis</h2>
<p>The example is evaluated as an oil development with infrastructure distance unspecified.
The local economic fallback is used in an isolated environment without the optional
external data package. Report calculations are explicitly skipped when that package is
installed; no backend is silently substituted. The fiscal
identifier is retained, but no tax adjustment is applied.</p>
<h3>4.1 System representation</h3>
<p>A floating spar host, production riser and seabed connection are shown schematically.
The drawing identifies the physical system only; hull dimensions, mooring geometry,
well count, pressure boundary conditions and metocean loads are not supplied.</p>
